# Humanaity Backend Best Practices

When working on this project, use repository-visible guidance and existing backend code structure as the source of truth.

## Mandatory: Read Before Suggesting

- Before suggesting code changes, refactors, architecture decisions, styling guidance, or commit messages, read relevant documentation that exists in this checkout and inspect nearby backend modules for established conventions.

## When To Read What

- For commit messages, review the repo diff first and follow conventional commit conventions already used in the repository history.
- For code changes, new features, and architecture questions, inspect the current backend package structure and use sprint/docs artifacts for implementation constraints.

## General Workflow

1. Check available docs in `docs/`.
2. Inspect related backend modules for existing patterns.
3. Apply those conventions contextually.
